# Halcora — full image package set.
#
# This list ends up BOTH in the live session and, because the installer unpacks
# the live squashfs, on the installed system. There is no separate target list,
# so anything a user needs after installing has to be here.
#
# "Full" is the image for a real desktop: 8 GB of RAM or more, a discrete GPU or
# a recent integrated one. It is the one that carries the whole theme, the store
# and the applications. The lite list lives beside this one.
#
# Deliberately absent: archinstall (we ship Calamares) and releng's rescue
# toolchain (irssi, nmap, testdisk, clonezilla and ~40 others). zsh is absent
# too, which is why /etc/passwd does not point root at it.

# --- base system ---
base
linux
linux-firmware
mkinitcpio
mkinitcpio-archiso
arch-install-scripts
sudo
nano

# --- filesystems and partitioning ---
btrfs-progs
dosfstools
e2fsprogs
exfatprogs
ntfsprogs
parted
gptfdisk
squashfs-tools

# --- boot ---
grub
efibootmgr
syslinux

# --- networking ---
networkmanager
iwd
wpa_supplicant

# --- audio ---
pipewire
pipewire-alsa
pipewire-pulse
pipewire-jack
wireplumber

# --- desktop ---
# plasma-meta pulls plasma-nm, plasma-pa, discover, print-manager, spectacle,
# xdg-desktop-portal-kde, kscreenlocker and the rest of the Plasma set, so only
# the extras are listed explicitly.
plasma-meta
sddm
xdg-user-dirs
xdg-utils
konsole
dolphin
kate
ark
gwenview
okular
kcalc
udisks2
gvfs
gvfs-mtp

# --- bluetooth ---
bluez
bluez-utils
bluez-obex

# --- printing ---
cups

# --- applications ---
firefox

# --- fonts ---
noto-fonts
noto-fonts-emoji
ttf-liberation
inter-font

# --- store ---
flatpak
packagekit-qt6

# --- installer ---
# Halcora installs itself now: /usr/local/bin/halcora-install is our own script,
# built from tools that already ship in the base system. What it needs is
# arch-install-scripts (genfstab, arch-chroot), squashfs-tools (unsquashfs),
# dosfstools, e2fsprogs, util-linux (sfdisk, lsblk, findmnt) and grub — all
# listed above. Adding them again here would be a comment pretending to be a
# dependency.
#
# What remains is the elevation path and the terminal the installer runs in.
polkit
polkit-kde-agent
konsole
